Instances of a mesh light authored with primvars:arnold:light, in nested point instancers

see #2193 and #2437

Same as test_2193, with a point instancer of a mesh light instanced by another point instancer. The Arnold instancer
doesn't render the instances of a mesh light made by a chain of instancers, so the render delegate flattens the nested
instances of mesh lights into a single instancer. The four instances light the grey ground, from the transforms of both
point instancers and the prototype's own transform: two elongated pools at the top left and two at the bottom right.
The legacy usd reader doesn't instance these mesh lights yet, the test is skipped in the 'usd' pass (see the
testsuite groups).

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'scene': 'scene.usda'}
